---
description: al-Rayhaanat Design System — always-on rules for any UI work
alwaysApply: true
---

This project uses `@al-rayhaanat/system` for all UI. These rules are enforced by
`@al-rayhaanat/config` and fail the build, not warn.

- Import components from `@al-rayhaanat/system`. Check the inventory in
  `AGENTS.md` before building anything — there are 153 exports.
- Never add another component or icon library. `lucide-react`, `react-icons`,
  `@heroicons/react` and `framer-motion` are `no-restricted-imports` errors.
  Icons come from `Icon` (carries RTL mirror flags), motion from `Transition` /
  `FadeIn` / `Collapse` / `Stagger` (handle `prefers-reduced-motion`).
- Never import package internals (`@al-rayhaanat/ui/src/*`) or dist paths
  (`@al-rayhaanat/tokens/dist/*`). Import the package root.
- Theme and direction come from `<html data-theme="light|dark" dir="ltr|rtl"
  lang="en|ar">` and nothing else. There is no provider, no context, no
  `useTheme()`, no `dark:` variant, no second palette.
- `@al-rayhaanat/system/tokens.css` is imported once, at the app root. On
  Next.js, `transpilePackages: ["@al-rayhaanat/system"]` is required — the
  packages ship source JSX.

Full reference: `AGENTS.md`.
